==Quest Walkthrough==
Depending on whether the player reported any of Team Rocket's crimes to the police during [[Quests|Team Rocket missions]] in [[Cerulean City]] or [[Celadon City]], this quest can be played from one of two teams: the Police or Team Rocket.

Regardless of the side chosen, for the duration of the quest, the player will lose access to their Pokémon and items; these will be returned when the player leaves the island. To complete the quest, the player must use the limited resources available to catch Pokémon in order to progress across the island.

===Police Side===
To start on the side of the police, the player must have reported at least one crime during any of the "No Fishing Zone", "Disobedient Pokémon" or "Pokémon Collector" missions. If they have done so, police officers will be standing outside the train station in [[Goldenrod City]]. While talking to them, they will ask the player help them out. The player can then depart from the docks near the Radio Tower.

The player will be given a level 15 Snubbull and an Emergency Whistle to start off with. The officer on the right side of the pier will heal the player's party and give the player 5 Poké Balls whenever the player has less than 5, and will give 5 DNA Splicers and 2 DNA Reversers whenever the player has less than 5 DNA Splicers.

The player may believe they are soft locked due to none of the gifted nor catch able Pokémon being able to learn either of the required HM's, however the can obtain a Igglyshrew (Igglybuff + Sandshrew Fusion) after speaking to the Team Rocket grunt on the left side of the island next to the black boat and then interacting with the Igglyshrew.

{{Stub}}

===Team Rocket Side===
To start on the side of Team Rocket, the player must go to Team Rocket's hideout in [[Goldenrod City|Goldenrod Tunnel]]. There they will be given the mission, and taken to a hidden dock where they can depart to Pinkan Island.

The player will be given a choice of a level 12 Ekans, Zubat or Koffing, and an Emergency Whistle to start off with. A grunt on the shore will heal the player's party and give the player 5 Rocket Balls whenever the player has less than 5, and will give 5 DNA Splicers and 2 DNA Reversers whenever the player has less than 5 DNA Splicers.

The player may believe they are soft locked due to none of the gifted nor catch able Pokémon being able to learn either of the required HM's, however the can obtain an Igglyran (Igglybuff + Nidoran Fusion) after talking to either of the two NPC's at the table in the house on the bottom right of the island and then interacting with the Igglyran. (Nevertheless, there does exist a way to get through the request without obtaining the Igglyran.)

